discussion among Board members, including participation from Plaintiff and questions from other

Board members about whether other structural issues had been identified and what kinds of

liability such issues might create, see id. at 9–10, the Board voted to “conduct an orderly wind-

down of programming activities through the Spring of 2026 and close [the Center’s] doors entirely


