       Mr. Buchalter explained that under the first proposal, the planned construction would

“[c]ost[] more and take[] longer.” Id. Delta projected that cost increases would mean that the $257

million appropriation would cover only roughly half of the necessary work. See id. Delta pointed

to recent revenue decline at the Center as evidence of “uncertainty and friction,” a decline that Mr.

Buchalter expected would continue over the course of the entire—longer—project timeframe. See

