       In fact, though Congresswoman Beatty voted against the August 13 measure, she explicitly

stated that she had “no objection” to one component of it—re-naming the Center’s grounds after

President Trump to honor the work he is doing to save the Kennedy Center.

       Without those efforts, the Center will deteriorate further into an unsafe, decrepit structure

that will be required to be taken down, with a determination to follow on what to build on the site,

