“any plaque on a theater chair or a theater box acknowledging the gift of such chair or box”; and
“any inscription on the marble walls in the north or south galleries, the Hall of States, or the Hall
of Nations acknowledging a major contribution,” “which plaque or inscription is permitted under
policies of the Board in effect on December 2, 1983.”
       2
          To the extent the renaming of the Center’s grounds differs from the other two proposed
