79, 80 n.21. A federal court has inherent authority to “clarify . . . the terms of the injunction
being appealed from.” Escobar Molina v. DHS, 832 F. Supp. 3d 22, 38 (D.D.C. 2026) (internal
quotation marks omitted); cf. Dunlap v. Presidential Advisory Comm’n on Election Integrity,
944 F.3d 945, 949 (D.C. Cir. 2019) (explaining an injunction is clarified rather than modified for
jurisdictional purposes if the parties could “have reasonably foreseen that the injunction extended
that far”).


                                                  6

---

