a term means the same thing throughout a statute “yields readily to indications that the same

phrase used in different parts of the same statute means different things, particularly where the

phrase is one that speakers can easily use in different ways without risk of confusion”). This

Court thus rejected a narrow, building-only definition of “the John F. Kennedy Center for the

Performing Arts.” “Physically,” the opinion accompanying the injunction explained, “the Center

is more than just a grand marble building overlooking the Potomac River. In addition to its

