provision makes sense only if “the John F. Kennedy Center for the Performing Arts” as used in

§ 76j(b) includes the campus—i.e., it refers to more than merely the main building. This reading

also gives meaning to words in the statute such as “building” that would be redundant if “the

John F. Kennedy Center for the Performing Arts” referred only to the main building. E.g., id.

§§ 76i(4), 76j(a)(1)(H)(ii), 76q-1(a)(4), 76s.

