than their present arguments let on. The resolution at issue, after all, was passed by the Board of

Trustees of the John F. Kennedy Center of the Performing Arts. As its name suggests, that entity

oversees the entire institution, not simply the main building. Otherwise, it would lack authority

to take any actions with respect to the grounds—a result the government surely would not

countenance.

