named for President Eisenhower, who originally championed the creation of a national cultural
center in Washington. But that designation occurred in 1968, before Congress’s 1983
amendment of the statute to prohibit “additional memorials” “after December 2, 1983.” 20
U.S.C. § 76j(b)(1); see Reply, ECF No. 70 at 9 & n.3 (citing Harold Gal, Theater in Kennedy

