“nominal party” standing in for some other “real party in interest.” Id. at 305 n.2 (Roberts, C.J.,

dissenting). She is a steward of the res, holding a legal interest in it that is “subject to an

equitable obligation to keep or use that interest for the” American public. Bogert’s Law on

Trusts § 1. And the legal rights she seeks to vindicate are “first-party, not third-party” ones.

