their challenges to Beatty’s Article III standing, which the Court has already rejected. Beatty’s

inability to administer the trust in accordance with its governing statute is an irreparable injury

that the Court cannot fix by awarding money damages or remedies available at law; only an

injunction prohibiting the Board from continuing to effectuate its unlawful decision will place

Beatty in good stead as to her statutory and fiduciary duties.23




