response to Representative Beatty’s TRO request, the record shows that most Board members

had received no document, plan, or even the vaguest of explanations for the proposed closure.

The documents disclosed to Beatty filled in some detail, but they focused largely on the

renovation work that the Board was already aware would take place, not the need to shutter the

Kennedy Center.30



