Borda Decl. ¶ 18; see also Taylor Decl. ¶ 15 (“If a closure is truly necessary, by the time it is
announced, the governing body should already have in hand extensive reports, cost analyses,
construction plans, and third-party validated budgets[.]”); Am. Amicus Br. at 4–8. Here, Board
members received, two days before the closure vote, a handful of vague documents penned by
Mr. Floca, a light-on-details budget document, and a few years-old CBPs and consultant reports.


